 "note": "PM run (second of the day). Checked 75, filed 4 facts across 4 people, each parent-verified on its source page and read back in the Sheet exactly once. Fresh sweep found three winners: Mark C Walczyk won re-election to the New York State Senate (49th District) with 69% of the vote over Cassie Robbins-Forbus (NCPR, published Nov 4, 2026); Janelle Evans scored a power-play goal in Clarkson's 3-1 win over Franklin Pierce on Oct 16, 2026 (Franklin Pierce University); and Kaitlyn Mallette scored in Clarkson's 6-1 win over Providence on Oct 24, 2026 (ECAC Hockey). The hot list carries Walczyk's win only \u2014 it is the one filed fact published Nov 3 or Nov 4. The compounding lane ran on 5 people (Zvi Szafran, Michelle Johnston, Ashleigh Graveline, Natalie Waterman, Eric Trelease): it filed one correction merge \u2014 the Arizona Occupational Therapy Association's 2025 program lists Graveline as OTD, PhD and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, now noted in her footprint text; her Degrees field was left as it is because Clarkson's own pages do not settle the doctorate \u2014 plus 8 likely finds went to the ledger and 10 chains circled back and confirmed facts already on file. Most other solid-looking rotation claims this run failed parent verification \u2014 dead or wrong source addresses, blocked pages, and one claimed award listing that is not on the page it was credited to \u2014 and were recorded in Research Command as unverified rather than filed. This run added 40 candidates to the Research Command ledger. 11 JD console filings were reconciled into changes.json. Unharvested photo leads flagged by JD in Research Command, awaiting a photo pass: Christine Sutter (UConn Today); Emily Criscitello (Tulum dive operator); Joann Duclos (Army.mil); Joe Charlebois (Hockey records); Katelyn Tomford (Zola); Kayla Hettel (Puget Sound Birth Center); Max Ferran (Bold.org); Megan Converse (Merit Pages).",
